00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:13.481
You know how easy it is
to find good employees?

00:07:13.481 --> 00:07:14.480
Let me explain.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:15.559
You go to Twitter search.

00:07:15.559 --> 00:07:17.799
You search the terms
around the job description

00:07:17.799 --> 00:07:19.899
that you want, not the
job description terms,

00:07:19.899 --> 00:07:21.663
but the kind of things they'd be doing.

00:07:21.663 --> 00:07:24.682
Looking at people talking
about design websites,

00:07:24.682 --> 00:07:26.540
design forums, design aspects,

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.722
and then looking around
what people are saying.

00:07:28.722 --> 00:07:30.138
Then clicking on their profile.

00:07:30.138 --> 00:07:31.194
Clicking their homepage.

00:07:31.194 --> 00:07:33.492
Probably landing on
their design portfolio.

00:07:33.492 --> 00:07:35.545
Finding four people that
you think do a good job.

00:07:35.545 --> 00:07:37.334
Emailing them or Tweeting at them saying,

00:07:37.334 --> 00:07:38.343
"Do you want to interview for a job?

00:07:38.343 --> 00:07:39.330
"Are you looking for a job?"

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:40.745
Three of the four say, "No."

00:07:40.745 --> 00:07:41.464
One says, "Yes."

00:07:41.464 --> 00:07:43.342
The other three give you four referrals

00:07:43.342 --> 00:07:44.305
